[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Thirteen Equals One]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.29]Lesson 2 | 第2课
[00:02.18]Thirteen equals one | 十三等于一
[00:10.10]Was the vicar pleased that the clock was striking? Why? | 教堂的钟敲响时牧师高兴吗？为什么？
[00:16.63]Our vicar is always raising money for one cause or another, | 我们的牧师总是为这样或那样的事业募捐，
[00:20.87]but he has never managed to get enough money to have the church clock repaired. | 但始终未能筹到足够的钱来修理教堂的大钟。
[00:26.49]The big clock which used to strike the hours day and night was damaged many years ago and has been silent ever since. | 那座曾经日夜报时的大钟多年前就坏了，从此便一直无声无息。
[00:36.38]One night, however, our vicar woke up with a start:the clock was striking the hours! | 然而一天夜里，我们的牧师猛然惊醒：大钟正在报时！
[00:43.48]Looking at his watch, he saw that it was one o'clock, | 他看了看表，才凌晨1点，
[00:47.38]but the bell struck thirteen times before it stopped. | 可那只钟竟连敲了13下才停。
[00:51.91]Armed with a torch, the vicar went up into the clock tower to see what was going on. | 牧师拿着一支手电筒上了钟楼，想去看个究竟。
[00:58.03]In the torchlight, he caught sight of a figure whom he immediately recognized as Bill Wilkins, our local grocer. | 借着手电光，他看见一个人影，立刻认出那是本地杂货店老板比尔·威尔金斯。
[01:06.24]'Whatever are you doing up here Bill?' asked the vicar in surprise. | “比尔，你到底在这上面干什么？”牧师惊讶地问。
[01:11.57]'I'm trying to repair the bell, ' answered Bill. | “我想把这口钟修好，”比尔回答说。
[01:15.23]'I've been coming up here night after night for weeks now. | “几个星期以来，我天天夜里往这儿跑。
[01:18.64]You see, I was hoping to give you a surprise.' | 你瞧，我就是想让你大吃一惊。”
[01:22.40]'You certainly did give me a surprise!' said the vicar. | “你确实让我吃了一惊！”牧师说。
[01:25.82]'You've probably woken up everyone in the village as well. | “说不定你还把全村的人都吵醒了。
[01:29.51]Still, I'm glad the bell is working again.' | 不过，我很高兴这口钟又能报时了。”
[01:33.01]'That's the trouble, vicar, 'answered Bill. 'It's working all right, | “麻烦就在这儿，牧师，”比尔回答说，“钟是能走了，
[01:38.07]but I'm afraid that at one o'clock it will strike thirteen times and there's nothing I can do about it.' | 可到了凌晨1点，它准会敲13下，我毫无办法。”
[01:45.01]'We'll get used to that, Bill, 'said the vicar. | “我们会习惯的，比尔，”牧师说。
[01:48.05]'Thirteen is not as good as one, but it's better than nothing. | “13下虽然不如1下好，但总比不敲强。
[01:52.95]Now let's go downstairs and have a cup of tea.' | 现在咱们下楼去喝杯茶吧。”
